module gunbc.plans.v2_compiler_architecture

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock, MarkdownTableRow, CodeBlock, TableBlock, AlignNone }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { h3, p, cell, row }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }

fn code(text: String) -> MarkdownBlock { CodeBlock { code: text } }

fn table3(header: MarkdownTableRow, rows: List<MarkdownTableRow>) -> MarkdownBlock {
  TableBlock { header: header, alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone], rows: rows }
}

fn r3(a: String, b: String, c: String) -> MarkdownTableRow { row(cells: [cell(text: a), cell(text: b), cell(text: c)]) }

fn v2_compiler_architecture_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "No implementation lands from this document. **Goal/authority:** v2 derives what the model determines, exposes only genuine unknowns and proves later forms agree with authored intent. This is the compiler architecture below DESIGN, established 2026-10-01; implementation still requires the domain models and owning stage work. gunbc.plan_governance alone owns the child relation; do not copy its inventory into plan bodies. The [original operator statements and review of 14f36a479f](https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/blob/3e5a0f1f0dbc62e0d3589df44146858d3147c9e9/dag/gunbc/plans/v2_compiler_architecture.dag) record provenance."),
    p(text: "**1. Completion law:** accept a partial authored program and compute its maximal unique lawful completion from types/sole constructors, selected realizations/upstream facts, catalogs, root policy, providers and observers. One preserving route completes; zero/multiple routes or a semantic change yield typed located residuals with provenance and addressee. Never search alternatives or consult ambient PATH/device/package defaults. Supplying a derivable fact is a second authority unless an explicit reasoned policy departure is admitted."),
    h3(text: "1.1 Completion is a partition of routes by type, never a search"),
    p(text: "**Route partition:** the hole’s type determines its route, not a preference order: placement from effect host binding; environmental values from the root’s subject-indexed provider; package coordinates from catalogs; artifacts from materialization judgment; grants from admission; leases from lease authority; facts from observers; representation crossings from coercion homomorphisms. Plain Int is never completed. Missing route inputs propagate as enclosing requirements. Select statically and carry provenance; never resolve by runtime type guessing."),
    h3(text: "1.2 A residual is a question with an addressee"),
    p(text: "**Residual ownership:** caller answers irreducible operation inputs; root answers policy/supplier/store/placement choices; upstream module answers unmodeled facts; observer answers world facts. Runtime refusals/contention are closed-program outcomes, not residuals. The addressee constrains complete calls too: a call-site value cannot override a root-owned answer. A test is a root and binds suppliers before expansion; replacing a whole supplier removes its acquisition subtree, replacing a dependency retains its callers. Selected graph/execution evidence supplies provenance without value-origin tags."),
    h3(text: "1.3 Closure: libraries may be open, runnable roots may not"),
    p(text: "**Closure:** a library exposes irreducible parameters plus inferred requirements. Runnable roots close every non-call-site residual. Runtime-only subjects must become static or use the addressed input/observer, never fallback. Cross-root suppliers expand under their own owner/authority and export exact subject-specific results; consumers only gain permitted observation. Join the exported secret/version/host/principal identity to the actual artifact read, not merely a file path. Only assigned managed suppliers enter desired state: observing a vendor or absence grants no ownership. Controls must show roster deletion leaves the requirement derived and supplier deletion refuses with its path (ensure_closure_design §14)."),
    h3(text: "1.4 Completion and coercion are one procedure"),
    p(text: "**Coercion:** completion, coercion and emission are directions of the same preserving decision procedure. A unique image is silent, a discharged modeled proof obligation is carried, and no unique preserving image yields an addressed residual. Implicit coercion must be total, exact, semantics-preserving, unique, pure and consent-free. Named conversion plans answer meaning mismatches; providers answer environmental requirements; neither substitutes for the other."),
    h3(text: "1.5 The one semantic addition, and two obligations beside it"),
    p(text: "**Semantic/admission frontier:** omitted-operand elaboration is the one language addition: exact application bijection holds after completion, with no new syntax. Complete applications also need the derivable-operand rule (omit or declare divergence). Provider-minted lifecycle provenance comes from sealed library carriers/domain admission, not demand derivation. Existing admit_callers/sole_constructor support does not imply full coverage: seed coproduct variants f13 and defaults f19 were residuals in the audit. The policy-departure form must exist before the derivable-operand rule rejects calls."),
    p(text: "**Measurement:** hold authored contract, route universe, root policy and observer surface fixed; AvoidableOverAsk must not increase. DiscoveredResidual from newly modeled behavior or candidates is a fidelity discovery, not regression. Total residual count is not monotone. Under-asking through ambient defaults is fail-open and forbidden."),
    p(text: "**2. Lenses:** pure readers over the same Node graph, storing nothing and never repairing what they find. dependency_fidelity compares declared dependencies with executed interactions; mutation_adequacy checks that relationship mutations are killed. Compare authored↔completed, declared↔consumed, completed↔realized, realized↔observed (readback/incarnation/freshness), claim↔execution and dependency↔interaction. Completion cannot guess and lenses cannot mask divergence."),
    code(text: "ingest → resolve/infer → completion fixed point\n→ producer-closed templates → admitted demand instances\n→ execute/evaluate/emit → observe and carry evidence"),
    p(text: "**3. Pipeline:** grammar ingest → Node/Edge core → resolve/infer → static completion fixed point → producer-closed plan → derived/minimized demand graph → execution/evaluation or target emission → observations/receipts/evidence. The fixed point binds logical placement/root policy, uniquely selects realization/provider/route, derives and completes prerequisites, then repeats. Zero/multiple routes and cycles without a base remain residuals. Before execution choose CLI/native SCM, principal, package/image/materialization route and grant admission; afterward allocate capacity/leases, materialize/reuse, redeem grants, effect, observe/reconcile and mint. A runtime-known requirement uses a statically admitted resolver demand checked before consumption, never a new semantic kind."),
    p(text: "**Closed schemas, lazy instances (2026-10-21):** producer-closed means every possible demand instantiates an admitted template with exactly one producer route, not that every instance has been enumerated. Recursive generation carries DescentEvidence; each produced fragment still undergoes cycle checks. Instances/fragments are immutable once instantiated, with complete reuse identity. Purity, immutability, well-founded expansion and identity completeness are separate obligations. Observations enter as values; resource claims remain effects. Regions complete/execute independently under local prerequisites; management computation is demand work. Seed/native realization bootstraps management, and a successor becomes eligible only after its full generation/realization contract is admitted (demand_engine_program D10); it cannot be needed to establish itself. “Sealed” retains population/read-set meanings. Current demand_engine_seal is the eager whole-population special case; lazy scheduling/compiler cuts belong to M3a–M6 and execution grain to that program §2.2."),
    p(text: "**4. Standing:** the retained table below is the original authority audit, not a fresh execution receipt. Completion/residual/closure were stated but unbuilt; environmental completion was the first designed vertical. Do not infer current implementation from the table."),
    table3(
      header: r3(a: "Stage", b: "Authority today", c: "Standing against the law"),
      rows: [
        r3(a: "DESIGN.md", b: "`gunbc.design_document`", c: "implicitly aligned: section 2 models once and derives every use, section 3 forbids second authorities, section 4 makes ingest, emit and coercion one procedure, section 5 refuses fallbacks; it does not yet state 'the author supplies only residuals' as one compiler law (section 7 below)"),
        r3(a: "grammar ingestion and emission", b: "the grammar rows read in both directions (DESIGN section 4); `extdeps.languages`", c: "strong pass: one grammar, forward for ingest and backward for emit"),
        r3(a: "application and type floor", b: "`v2.compiler` infer; DESIGN section 4b floor", c: "the current blocker: exact argument bijection treats an omitted operand as an error; elaboration of omitted operands is the one semantic addition (1.5)"),
        r3(a: "coercion", b: "`v2.std.coercion`, `v2.std.inhabitance`", c: "strong kernel, incomplete architecture: witness-or-typed-mismatch already, no addressee and no whole-program placement yet (1.4)"),
        r3(a: "completion, residual and closure", b: "this document, section 1", c: "stated; unbuilt; its environmental specialization is the first vertical"),
        r3(a: "demand derivation and the demand engine", b: "`gunbc.plans.demand_engine_program` (D1-D13), `v2.std.demand_engine`", c: "strong pass within scope: ordinary sequential programs induce demands and relations without feature-authored rows"),
        r3(a: "materialization", b: "`std.materialization_ladder`, `v2.std.materialize`", c: "conceptually strong, unevenly applied: derives recurrence and provider obligations; the rule that the compiler reports only why reuse cannot be decided is not yet positioned above it"),
        r3(a: "environmental completion", b: "`gunbc.plans.ensure_closure_design` (D14)", c: "strong design, not yet substrate: the developer supplies residuals, the host closure is derived, ensure is one mechanism, no syntax duplicates structure"),
        r3(a: "CLI and realization", b: "`extdeps.exec`, `gunbc.command_runner`, `gunbc.cli_dispatch_surface`", c: "mixed: raw program spellings, independently supplied packages and ambient execution routes remain (the D14 census)"),
        r3(a: "deployment layout", b: "D14 section 3.3", c: "strong proposed model: small provider-family policy at the root, large concrete closure derived per executable"),
        r3(a: "dependency relations", b: "`v2.std.dependency`", c: "partially aligned: structural, execution and provenance readings are unevenly integrated; D14's relation step owns the projection"),
        r3(a: "lenses", b: "`v2.lens.dependency_fidelity`, `v2.lens.mutation_adequacy`", c: "strong capability, weak placement: they are the reflective half (section 2) and no compiler-root design said so until this one"),
        r3(a: "diagnostics", b: "typed, located refusals throughout", c: "partial: a uniform residual with provenance, addressee and available answer routes is not yet universal"),
        r3(a: "plan document graph", b: "`gunbc.plan_registry`, now `gunbc.plan_governance`", c: "was a fail -- plans were inventoried, not placed; the relation and its lens claims land with this document (section 6)"),
      ]
    ),
    p(text: "**5. Specializations:** ensure_closure_design owns environmental targets/provider families/host blueprint/lifecycle; demand_engine_program owns demand identity, minimization and realization/materialization/placement specialization, consuming the completed program rather than owning omission. Coercion’s frontier is addressed mismatch plus named conversion plans and a first Rust/TypeScript core-module mismatch instrument. Materialization reports why reuse cannot be established; tolerated staleness is its world-read residual. CLI surface is exactly residual decisions; derivable flags are counted defects. Evidence remains cross-cutting."),
    p(text: "**6. Plan graph:** plan_governance_rows declares the one irreducible child→governor/role relation; plan_to_blocks derives banners and child lists. Admission mints a sole-constructor functional, rooted, acyclic, complete graph with typed defects; every projection/lens consumes it, never first-match rows. Controls include two parents, duplicate same parent, governed root, hidden cycles in both orders, cycle, orphan and ordinary chain. plan_governance_witness checks registered endpoints/root and root reachability. Top-down/backlink projection waits for a second governance level; exactly-one-stage-authority/frontier waits for stage rows; ancestor-law duplication detection waits for a semantic body lens, not grep."),
    p(text: "**7–8. Remaining decisions:** carry the compact completion ruling through gunbc.design_document, never hand-edit its DESIGN projection; place mechanisms here until typed stage/carrier authorities replace them. Decide CompilerStage rows and their authority/frontier totality, policy-departure spelling (ensure_closure_design §15), and whether governance references stage declarations once modeled. The retirement condition below requires executing elaboration/residual/closure carriers and stage-governance witnesses, not merely a shorter statement of the law."),
  ]
}

data v2_compiler_architecture_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
  slug: "v2-compiler-architecture",
  title: "v2 compiler architecture: completion, residual, closure, and the lenses that prove them",
  body: v2_compiler_architecture_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Delete this document when the law of its section 1 is carried by gunbc.design_document as a ruling and by the compiler's own carriers -- elaboration of omitted operands on the floor, residuals as a typed carrier with provenance and addressee consumed by every stage's refusal path, closure refused at runnable roots -- and when the stage roster of its section 4 is rows with one authority or one explicit frontier each, enrolled under the plan-governance lens. At that point the carriers, the stage rows and their witnesses are the authority for the architecture, and this document would be a second statement of it.") }
}
